ire i think this  flexibility of supply  if the mix and match strategy addresses  that researchers say it would be a major  step  forward but it could also lead to  enhanced immunity  while all of the vaccines target the  spike protein  they focus on different locations in  that region  so mixing doses may possibly provide  broader spectrum immunity this is not a  crazy idea that suddenly just come up  because we're  so desperate for vaccines for covid this  is actually something that  immunologically makes sense  vaccines for ebola tb and malaria are  already based on the mix and match  concept  while widely used in other disease  treatments  the uk study is the only one underway  looking  at covid19 vaccines something that  surprises this saben vaccine institute  leader  like the rest of this response we want  this to be the best science-based  response as possible  and it'll be important to know if a  followed by b  is as good as a followed by a or vice  versa  i'm due to get my second shot my boost  in one or two months i hope  i hope the trial is done by the time  it's time for me to get my boost  and i can i can have that option or at  least talk to my physician  about which vaccine i should come in  with both dr bernstein  and barrett say there are conversations  about a similar trial  starting in canada results from the uk  trial  are expected this summer crystal  gomencing global news  london still ahead a deadly blast in  indonesia  just as holy week begins  just in case you were wondering that  ship in the suez canal  well it's moved but it's still stuck the  ever given did nudge a few degrees  saturday night but  that's about as far as it got it's now  on its sixth day blocking the vital  trade route  about 14 tugboats are still trying to  dislodge the ship but they don't seem to  be getting anywhere  over 300 ships are waiting on either  side of the canal to pass  causing a major disruption to the global  shipping network  myanmar's military isn't backing down  from its crackdown on protests despite  condemnation from around the world  [Music]  there are reports soldiers shot mourners  who gathered at a funeral for a student  killed yesterday  the bloodiest day of the coup at least  114 people died  including children protesters have  returned to the streets but there were  no large-scale demonstrations indonesia  is on edge tonight after a suicide  bombing during a palm sunday church  service  the blast happened just as mass was  ending on the first day of the easter  holy week  at least 20 people were hurt and taken  to hospital police say the two suspected  suicide bombers  died a security guard tried to stop them  from entering the grounds on a motorbike  indonesia's president condemned the  attack as an act of terrorism  up next how one american city is  addressing discriminatory housing  policies  [Music]  the canadian government is planning to  apologize to an all-black military unit  that served in the first world war the  number two construction battalion was  formed in 1916.  there were 600 men in the battalion half  of them were from nova scotia  they had volunteered to go to battle but  were turned away  because of the color of their skin but  they did build and maintain  critical infrastructure for canada's war  efforts in a virtual ceremony today  marking 104 years since their first  deployment  the defense minister says the country  owes them more than just gratitude  all the members their families  their communities an apology for the  racism and discrimination  they endured before during and long  after their service to canada the  effects of which  are still being filled a century after  the war ended  correcting the wrongs of the past begins  with acknowledging them  one city in the u.s is going a step  further evanston illinois has decided to  pay  reparations to black residents who faced  decades of discriminatory housing  policies  as jackson proskow reports it's the  beginning of a national 